---
layout: page.njk
title: Hexagon's Blog
description: "Hexagon writes about open source projects like Croner, rootcard and Murmo, and about Rust, JavaScript, Linux servers and security."
tags: index
---
<section class="mb-5">
    <h1 class="mb-3 hello">Hello, I'm Hexagon</h1>
    <span class="index-avatar"><img src="/img/hexagon_150.webp" width="150" height="150" alt="Hexagon's avatar" title="Hexagon's Avatar"></span>
    <p class="lead-text">I've been building things for the web since 1996, and releasing them as open source for most of that time. My best-known project is <a href="https://croner.56k.guru" target="_blank">Croner</a>, a cron scheduler that started in JavaScript and now exists for Rust, Python, .NET and C++, all following the <a href="https://github.com/open-source-cron/ocps" target="_blank">Open Cron Pattern Standard</a>. Lately I've been working on <a href="https://github.com/rootcard/rootcard" target="_blank">rootcard</a>, a federated identity where the server never sees your password, and <a href="https://murmo.org" target="_blank">Murmo</a>, an end-to-end encrypted messenger built on top of it.</p>
    <p>The blog covers what I happen to be working on: Rust and JavaScript, runtimes like Deno, Linux servers, security and identity, and letting AI help out with the day-to-day running of things. I'm all about Open Source, portable code and minimal bloat.</p>
    <p>Looking for something longer? Check out the series <a href="/posts/guide-to-rust/introduction/">The guide to Rust</a>, <a href="/posts/guide-to-js/introduction/">The guide to JavaScript</a> and <a href="/posts/ssh-keys-passwordless-login/">SSH keys and passwordless login</a>.</p>
    <p>This blog is built using <a href="https://deno.land" target="_blank">Deno</a> and <a href="https://lume.land" target="_blank">Lume</a>, and the source code is available at <a href="https://github.com/hexagon/blog">github.com/hexagon/blog</a>.</p>
    <br>
    <hr>
    <h2 class="mb-4 mt-5 section-title">Recent posts</h2>
    <div class="post-list">
    {% for subpost in search.pages("post", "date=desc", 20) %}
           
            <section>
                <hgroup>
                    <h3 class="post-title"><a href="{{ subpost.url }}">{{ subpost.title or "title" }}</a></h3>
                    <p>
                        <!-- Author -->
                        {% if subpost.author %}
                            by <strong>{{ subpost.author.name }}</strong>, 
                        {% endif %}

                        <!-- Date -->
                        <time datetime="{{ subpost.date | date("yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss'.000'XX") }}">
                            {{ subpost.date | date }}</time>{% if subpost.updated %}<span>, Updated:</span>
                        <time datetime="{{ subpost.updated | date("yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss'.000'XX") }}">
                            {{ subpost.updated | date }}
                        </time>
                        {% endif %}
                    </p>
                </hgroup>
                <p>
                    {{ subpost.intro | md | safe }}
                </p>
            </section>
    {% endfor %}
    </div>
</section>